§ `ss 4, 6 and 16`

#ASSERT `the Act applies to the mediation` `a neighbour dispute mediated in Singapore in 2024`
#ASSERT NOT `the Act applies to the mediation` `an oral agreement to mediate never recorded in any form`
#ASSERT `the Act applies to the mediation` `a mediation abroad under a Singapore-law clause`
#ASSERT NOT `the Act applies to the mediation` `a mediation abroad with no Singapore link`
#ASSERT NOT `the Act applies to the mediation` `a mediation run under a statutory scheme`
#ASSERT NOT `the Act applies to the mediation` `a court-directed mediation`
#ASSERT NOT `the Act applies to the mediation` `a mediation begun in 2016 and settled before November 2017`
#ASSERT `the Act applies to the mediation` `a mediation begun in 2017, still open, all agreeing to the Act`
#ASSERT NOT `the Act applies to the mediation` `a mediation begun in 2017, still open, one party not agreeing`
#ASSERT `the Act applies to the mediation` `a mediation begun on 1 November 2017`

§ `s 8`

#ASSERT `a stay may be applied for` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a stay may be applied for` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a stay may be applied for` FALSE TRUE TRUE

§ `s 9`

#ASSERT `the ground is in section 9(2)` `consent of all parties, the maker being a party`
#ASSERT `the ground is in section 9(2)` `consent of all parties and of the non-party maker`
#ASSERT NOT `the ground is in section 9(2)` `consent of all parties but not of the non-party maker`
#ASSERT NOT `the ground is in section 9(2)` `consent of some parties only`
#ASSERT `the ground is in section 9(2)` `the content was already public`
#ASSERT NOT `the ground is in section 9(2)` `the content is public only through an unlawful leak`
#ASSERT `the ground is in section 9(2)` `to prevent abuse or neglect of a child`
#ASSERT NOT `the ground is in section 9(2)` `research that identifies the speaker`
#ASSERT `the ground is in section 9(2)` `to seek legal advice`
#ASSERT `the ground is in section 9(2)` `the communication relates to an offence`
#ASSERT NOT `the ground is in section 9(2)` `to tell a journalist`

#ASSERT `the disclosure is permitted` `another party to the mediation` `no particular reason` FALSE
#ASSERT `the disclosure is permitted` `the mediator` `to embarrass the other side` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the disclosure is permitted` `a third party` `to tell a journalist` FALSE
#ASSERT `the disclosure is permitted` `a third party` `to tell a journalist` TRUE
#ASSERT `the disclosure is permitted` `a third party` `to seek legal advice` FALSE

§ `ss 10 and 11`

#ASSERT NOT `the communication may be admitted in evidence` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the communication may be admitted in evidence` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `the communication may be admitted in evidence` TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT `where to apply for permission` `in court proceedings` EQUALS `the court hearing the proceedings`
#ASSERT `where to apply for permission` `in arbitral proceedings` EQUALS `the arbitral tribunal hearing the proceedings`
#ASSERT `where to apply for permission` `in no pending proceedings` EQUALS `the General Division of the High Court`

§ `s 12`

#ASSERT `the application may be made` `a signed settlement by a certified mediator, applied for in week 6`
#ASSERT `the application may be made` `the same, applied for in week 8`
#ASSERT NOT `the application may be made` `the same, applied for in week 10 without an extension`
#ASSERT `the application may be made` `the same, applied for in week 10 with an extension`
#ASSERT NOT `the application may be made` `a settlement reached after a lawsuit was filed`
#ASSERT NOT `the application may be made` `a settlement where one party withholds consent`

#ASSERT `the court may record it` `a signed settlement by a certified mediator, applied for in week 6`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may record it` `the same, applied for in week 10 without an extension`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may record it` `a settlement by an uncertified mediator outside any designated provider`
#ASSERT `the court may record it` `a settlement administered by a designated provider with an uncertified mediator`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may record it` `an unsigned settlement`
#ASSERT `the court may record it` `a settlement obtained by duress`

#ASSERT NOT `the court may refuse to record it` `a signed settlement by a certified mediator, applied for in week 6`
